'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_bench_detect.spin2
''   Purpose.... A/B board-detection sweep -- characterise getBoardType() across all six pin
''               groups, on a Rev B rig and then on a Rev A rig, from one identical binary
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 11 Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 11 Sep 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHY THIS IS ITS OWN BINARY

  The main bench harness contains motion tests. Loading it on the Rev A rig puts a menu
  between an unprotected board and a spinning motor. This binary has NO MOTION CODE
  COMPILED IN AT ALL in its default build -- that is the guard, and it is a better guard
  than discipline. It also makes the two runs diffable line-for-line: no menu, no runtime
  branch, one fixed sequence start to finish.

  THE REV A BOARDS ARE ONE-SHOT. They are at risk precisely because the protection that
  would make them safe -- correct revision detection feeding rSenseForBoard, 5 ohm vs
  150 ohm, a 30x current-scaling swing -- is the broken thing. So Rev A protection needs
  the Rev A data. This over-captures on purpose; a thin run leaves us stuck in that loop.

  HOW IT IS RUN

      cd src
      ../tools/bench-run.sh <tier>          ' echoes the two commands; run them by hand

  or directly:

      pnut-ts -l -d -D BENCH_CFG test_bench_detect.spin2
      pnut-term-ts -r test_bench_detect.bin --console-mode --exit-on-end-session

  Two systems side by side, identically wired, both dual 6.5" with two boards each.
  Connect to the Rev B boards, run, capture the log; disconnect, connect to the Rev A
  boards, run the SAME binary, capture. Both logs come back for comparison.

  BUILD VARIANTS

    (default)           phase 1 only. Fully passive. NO OBJ reference to isp_bldc_motor,
                        therefore provably zero driver PASM2 in the image, therefore
                        physically incapable of starting a driver cog.
    -D BENCH_CFG        selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2. Required. A log
                        whose BD-CFG does not read cfg_id,BENCH is VOID.
    -D DETECT_PHASE2    adds phase 2 -- the poisoning probe. Links isp_bldc_motor and
                        starts a REAL DRIVER COG at commanded zero. MOTORS MUST BE
                        PHYSICALLY UNPLUGGED.
    -D DETECT_NO_TAIL   sweeps only the four electrically-safe groups, dropping the two
                        gate-adjacent tail groups. Use for a rail-ON run.
    -D DETECT_RAIL_ON   optional. States in the log that the motor rail was powered.
    -D DETECT_RAIL_OFF  optional. States in the log that the motor rail was not powered.

  THE GATE ON PHASE 2 IS COMPILE-TIME AND ONLY COMPILE-TIME. There is no keypress, no
  timeout and no runtime branch anywhere in this binary. Stephen types the compile command
  at the bench himself, seconds before the run, so -D DETECT_PHASE2 is a deliberate
  operator act at the moment it matters -- and its absence makes motion impossible rather
  than merely unlikely. A keypress can be fumbled; an absent compile flag cannot produce
  motion.

  RECORD DISCIPLINE

  Tag-first, comma-separated name,value pairs, all tags beginning BD-. Fixed-field: every
  record type always emits every field in the same order, never conditionally omitted.
  Absence is a TOKEN value (NEVER, NOMEAS, NA, NOLIB), never a missing field and never 0.
  That is what makes the A/B diff work line-for-line. No debug() ever appears inside a
  measured interval -- every repeat's numbers go into a VAR long array and the whole
  cell's records emit after the last repeat.

  Records are assembled into a byte buffer and emitted with a single debug(zstr_()) each,
  because a pnut-ts DEBUG statement carries at most 255 bytes of debug data and the wider
  records overrun that by a factor of three. One record is therefore always exactly one
  line, which is what the line-for-line A/B diff depends on.

  HAZARD: every read of a driver-owned pin here is pinread() (the IN register). There is
  no RDPIN and no RQPIN anywhere in this file -- the hazard is avoided by construction
  rather than by care.
}

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' every top in this tree runs at 270 MHz
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ

CON { build identity }

' Hand-bumped whenever this file changes, so a stale binary is visible in the log.
    SRC_REV     = 2
    FMT_VERSION = 1                                         ' BD-BANNER record-format version

' DETECT_PHASE2 implies DETECT_LIB: if phase 2 is compiled, the library must be linked
#ifdef DETECT_PHASE2
#define DETECT_LIB
#endif


CON { local pin-group base table }

' DELIBERATE LOCAL COPY of the library's PINS_* enum, and the one place guide rule 2.4
' (never copy an object's constants) is knowingly set aside. The default build has no OBJ
' reference to isp_bldc_motor at all, so motor.PINS_* is not nameable there -- yet the
' sweep must still name all six groups. The copy is not trusted: BD-ENUM cross-checks
' every one of these against the library's own value whenever the library IS linked, and
' a single mismatch voids the run.
'  GRP_P0_P15   - left board on the bench; base pin 0
'  GRP_P8_P23   - overlaps both boards; base pin 8; tail group
'  GRP_P16_P31  - right board on the bench; base pin 16
'  GRP_P24_P39  - PINS_NO_USE_P24_P39; not a legal base; base pin 24; tail group
'  GRP_P32_P47  - unpopulated on the bench; base pin 32
'  GRP_P40_P55  - unpopulated on the bench; base pin 40
    GRP_P0_P15  = 0
    GRP_P8_P23  = 8
    GRP_P16_P31 = 16
    GRP_P24_P39 = 24
    GRP_P32_P47 = 32
    GRP_P40_P55 = 40

    GROUP_COUNT      = 6
    TAIL_GROUP_COUNT = 2                                    ' P8_P23 and NO_USE_P24_P39, swept last
    NO_GROUP         = -1                                   ' "no group" / "no cog" sentinel
    LIB_ABSENT       = -1                                   ' library object not linked into this build

CON { pin-field geometry }

' R1: ADDPINS cannot cross a 32-pin port boundary -- 24 addpins 15 silently wraps to
' 24..31 plus 0..7, which for PINS_NO_USE_P24_P39 would have read (and pinclear'd) the
' LEFT board's P0-P7, its ADC and hall pins. Every 16-pin operation in this file is
' therefore split into two 8-pin operations, uniformly, for all six groups, with no
' special-casing. 24..31 and 32..39 each sit within their own group of 32.
    HALF_GROUP_SPAN  = 7                                    ' addpins operand: 8 pins
    GROUP_HI_OFFSET  = 8                                    ' second half of a 16-pin group
    HIGH_HALF_SHIFT  = 8                                    ' pre/post: high half into bits 8-15
    SENSE_PIN_OFFSET = 4                                    ' pinbase + 4, exactly as getBoardType()
    PWM_W_L_OFFSET   = 12                                   ' pin_pwm_w_l is pinbase + 12
    GROUP_SPAN       = 16                                   ' pins per motor pin group

CON { measurement parameters }

' N_REP is a detection probability, not a round number. The modes being chased are
' intermittent flips; for a 1-in-10 mode the chance of missing it entirely in one cell is
' 0.9^N -- 12% at N=20, 3.4% at N=32. A 1-in-8 chance of a clean-looking cell that is
' actually lying is how you end up back at a one-shot bench. 32 is also a power of two.
    N_REP            = 32                                   ' repeats per passive cell
    N_LIVE           = 8                                    ' repeats per cell with a driver cog RUNNING
    SUM_ITER         = 500                                  ' the library's own pinread count
    PROBE_MAX_ITER   = 2_000                                ' first-low probe ceiling
    BOUNCE_SAMPLES   = 64                                   ' samples taken after first-low
    CAL_ITER         = 500                                  ' poll-loop calibration iterations
    CHARGE_MS        = 1                                    ' the library's own waitms(1)
    REVB_SUM_LIMIT   = 250                                  ' pinSum > this reads as "not detected"
    REVB_MIN_US      = 20                                   ' high time below this reads as "not detected" (library DETECT_REVB_MIN_US)
    USEC_PER_SEC     = 1_000_000                            ' converts CLKFREQ to ticks per microsecond
    SETTLE_MS        = 200                                  ' let a started driver cog reach steady state

' The calibration pin is held DRIVEN HIGH so the poll loop can never exit early. P44 is
' PINS_P40_P55's sense pin, inside the commented-out LA header range -- nothing is
' connected there, and every sweep already drives it high for a millisecond anyway.
    ' The calibration pin is DRIVEN HIGH for CAL_ITER iterations, so it must be a pin that is
    ' electrically dead on this rig. It was GRP_P40_P55 + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET = P44 -- which, with
    ' the boards where they actually are (RIGHT P16_P31, LEFT P32_P47, measured 2026-09-11), is
    ' 32 + 12 = the LEFT board's pin_pwm_w_l gate-driver input. Driving a gate input high for
    ' the whole calibration is not something to do to a populated board.
    ' P15 is outside both board ranges on this rig and inside the empty PINS_P0_P15 group.
    ' isCalPinSafe() re-checks that at runtime against the DECLARED bases and refuses to
    ' calibrate if the assumption ever stops holding.
    CAL_PIN = 15

    CAL_IDX_PRE_PHASE1  = 1
    CAL_IDX_POST_PHASE1 = 2
    CAL_IDX_POST_PHASE2 = 3

CON { record assembly buffer }

    LINE_BUF_SIZE   = 640                                   ' widest record is well under this
    MAX_DEC_DIGITS  = 11                                    ' a 32-bit value needs at most 10
    DEC_RADIX       = 10
    DIGITS_PER_GROUP = 3                                    ' underscore every three digits
    HEX4_DIGITS     = 4
    BITS_PER_NIBBLE = 4
    NIBBLE_MASK     = $F

CON { sweep identifiers }

' The 8-sweep matrix. One fixed unconditional sequence; sweeps 3-8 exist only in the
' -D DETECT_PHASE2 build.
'  SW_COLD_NOCLR        - phase 1, all groups, N_REP, no cog ever, not pinclear'd
'  SW_COLD_CLR          - phase 1, all groups, N_REP, no cog ever, pinclear'd
'  SW_LIVE_LEFT         - phase 2, P0_P15 only, N_LIVE, driver cog RUNNING on P0_P15
'  SW_STOPPED_LEFT      - phase 2, all groups, N_REP, cog on P0_P15 STOPPED, not pinclear'd
'  SW_STOPPED_CLR_LEFT  - phase 2, all groups, N_REP, cog on P0_P15 STOPPED, pinclear'd
'  SW_LIVE_RIGHT        - phase 2, P16_P31 only, N_LIVE, driver cog RUNNING on P16_P31
'  SW_STOPPED_RIGHT     - phase 2, all groups, N_REP, cog on P16_P31 STOPPED, not pinclear'd
'  SW_STOPPED_CLR_RIGHT - phase 2, all groups, N_REP, cog on P16_P31 STOPPED, pinclear'd
    #1, SW_COLD_NOCLR, SW_COLD_CLR, SW_LIVE_LEFT, SW_STOPPED_LEFT, SW_STOPPED_CLR_LEFT, ...
        SW_LIVE_RIGHT, SW_STOPPED_RIGHT, SW_STOPPED_CLR_RIGHT

CON { cell axis codes }

' Cog-state axis of the 2x2x2 matrix:
'  CST_NONE     - no driver cog has ever run in this power cycle
'  CST_RUNNING  - a driver cog is running on the cell's own group right now
'  CST_STOPPED  - a driver cog ran on some group and has been stop()ped
    #0, CST_NONE, CST_RUNNING, CST_STOPPED

' pinclear axis of the 2x2x2 matrix:
'  CLR_NO   - pins left exactly as the previous sweep left them
'  CLR_YES  - every swept group pinclear'd before this sweep
    #0, CLR_NO, CLR_YES

' Verdict codes -- the replica's, the library's, and the per-cell modal value:
'  VRD_REVA     - pinSum == 0
'  VRD_REVB     - pinSum in 1..REVB_SUM_LIMIT and high time >= REVB_MIN_US
'  VRD_NODET    - pinSum > REVB_SUM_LIMIT, or high time < REVB_MIN_US, "Board not detected!"
'  VRD_TIE      - per-cell modal only: no single verdict held a majority
'  VRD_UNKNOWN  - library returned something outside REV_A/REV_B/REV_Unknown
'  VRD_NOBASE   - group is not a legal base, so getBoardType() never measured
'  VRD_ABORT    - the library call aborted with a value
'  VRD_NOLIB    - the library object is not linked into this build
    #0, VRD_REVA, VRD_REVB, VRD_NODET, VRD_TIE, VRD_UNKNOWN, VRD_NOBASE, VRD_ABORT, VRD_NOLIB

' Pin-overlap classification for a group's sense pin:
'  OVL_SELF       - the sense pin belongs to this group's own configured board
'  OVL_NONE       - the sense pin is inside no configured board's range
'  OVL_LEFT_PWM   - the sense pin is the LEFT board's base+12, its W low-side gate input
'  OVL_RIGHT_PWM  - the sense pin is the RIGHT board's base+12, its W low-side gate input
'  OVL_OTHER      - overlaps a configured board at some other offset (non-bench config)
    #0, OVL_SELF, OVL_NONE, OVL_LEFT_PWM, OVL_RIGHT_PWM, OVL_OTHER

CON { build-variant flags }

#ifdef DETECT_NO_TAIL
    TAIL_GROUPS_ON = 0
#else
    TAIL_GROUPS_ON = 1
#endif

#ifdef DETECT_PHASE2
    PHASE2_COMPILED = 1
#else
    PHASE2_COMPILED = 0
#endif

#ifdef DETECT_LIB
    LIB_LINKED = 1
#else
    LIB_LINKED = 0
#endif

' rail_declared is an operator statement carried into the log, not a measurement. It is
' UNDECLARED unless the operator says otherwise at compile time. pnut-ts silently ignores
' an unknown -D, so a typo lands on UNDECLARED -- the honest default -- rather than on a
' confident lie. The objective evidence is elsewhere: bits 5,6,7 of a BD-REP pre field are
' pin_hall_u/v/w, so with a motor plugged in a valid 3-bit hall code proves the rail is up.
'  RAIL_UNDECLARED - operator said nothing
'  RAIL_ON         - built with -D DETECT_RAIL_ON
'  RAIL_OFF        - built with -D DETECT_RAIL_OFF
    #0, RAIL_UNDECLARED, RAIL_ON, RAIL_OFF

#ifdef DETECT_RAIL_ON
    RAIL_DECLARED = RAIL_ON
#elseifdef DETECT_RAIL_OFF
    RAIL_DECLARED = RAIL_OFF
#else
    RAIL_DECLARED = RAIL_UNDECLARED
#endif

    SWEPT_GROUP_COUNT = GROUP_COUNT - ((1 - TAIL_GROUPS_ON) * TAIL_GROUP_COUNT)

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"             ' bench compile-time hardware config (-D BENCH_CFG)
#else
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"                   ' active compile-time hardware config
#endif
#ifdef DETECT_LIB
    motor   : "isp_bldc_motor"                              ' linked when DETECT_LIB is set; DETECT_PHASE2 implies DETECT_LIB
#endif

DAT { sweep and enumeration order }

' Sweep order: the four electrically-safe groups first, the two gate-adjacent groups as a
' clearly-marked tail, so an aborted run still has the valuable data in the log.
grpSweepOrder   LONG    GRP_P0_P15, GRP_P16_P31, GRP_P32_P47, GRP_P40_P55, GRP_P8_P23, GRP_P24_P39

' Enumeration order: ascending base pin, used by the BD-ENUM and BD-MAP static tables.
grpEnumOrder    LONG    GRP_P0_P15, GRP_P8_P23, GRP_P16_P31, GRP_P24_P39, GRP_P32_P47, GRP_P40_P55

DAT { record assembly state }

lineBuf         BYTE    0[LINE_BUF_SIZE]
lineLen         LONG    0

DAT { record token strings }

sGrpP0P15       BYTE    "P0_P15", 0
sGrpP8P23       BYTE    "P8_P23", 0
sGrpP16P31      BYTE    "P16_P31", 0
sGrpP24P39      BYTE    "NO_USE_P24_P39", 0
sGrpP32P47      BYTE    "P32_P47", 0
sGrpP40P55      BYTE    "P40_P55", 0

sVrdRevA        BYTE    "REVA", 0
sVrdRevB        BYTE    "REVB", 0
sVrdNoDet       BYTE    "NODET", 0
sVrdTie         BYTE    "TIE", 0
sVrdUnknown     BYTE    "UNKNOWN", 0
sVrdNoBase      BYTE    "NOBASE", 0
sVrdAbort       BYTE    "ABORT", 0
sVrdNoLib       BYTE    "NOLIB", 0

sCstNone        BYTE    "NONE", 0
sCstRunning     BYTE    "RUNNING", 0
sCstStopped     BYTE    "STOPPED", 0

sClrNo          BYTE    "NOCLR", 0
sClrYes         BYTE    "CLR", 0

sOvlSelf        BYTE    "SELF", 0
sOvlNone        BYTE    "NONE", 0
sOvlLeftPwm     BYTE    "P0_P15+12_PWM_W_L", 0
sOvlRightPwm    BYTE    "P16_P31+12_PWM_W_L", 0
sOvlOther       BYTE    "OVL_OTHER", 0

sRailOn         BYTE    "ON", 0
sRailOff        BYTE    "OFF", 0
sRailUndecl     BYTE    "UNDECLARED", 0

sFlagTrue       BYTE    "1", 0
sFlagFalse      BYTE    "0", 0
sTokNA          BYTE    "NA", 0
sTokNever       BYTE    "NEVER", 0
sTokNoMeas      BYTE    "NOMEAS", 0
sTokUnknown     BYTE    "UNKNOWN", 0
sTokAll         BYTE    "ALL", 0

sExitLow        BYTE    "LOW", 0
sExitMaxed      BYTE    "MAXED", 0

sCfgBench       BYTE    "BENCH", 0
sCfgUser        BYTE    "USER", 0
sCfgFileBench   BYTE    "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench", 0
sCfgFileUser    BYTE    "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig", 0

sGateCompiled   BYTE    "COMPILED", 0
sGateNotComp    BYTE    "NOTCOMPILED", 0
sPhase2Ran      BYTE    "RAN", 0

sMarkBegin      BYTE    "begin", 0
sMarkEnd        BYTE    "end", 0
sMarkSkipped    BYTE    "skipped", 0
sMarkBuild      BYTE    "build", 0

sPh2Pre         BYTE    "pre", 0
sPh2Starting    BYTE    "starting", 0
sPh2Running     BYTE    "running", 0
sPh2Stopping    BYTE    "stopping", 0
sPh2Stopped     BYTE    "stopped", 0
sPh2Started     BYTE    "started", 0

VAR { per-cell measurement capture }

' One slot per repeat. Filled silently during the measured passes; read back only after
' the last repeat of a cell, so no debug() ever lands inside a measured interval.
    LONG    measured_sum[N_REP]                             ' the library's own 500-pinread sum
    LONG    measured_sum_ticks[N_REP]                       ' getct() ticks spanning that sum loop
    LONG    measured_iter[N_REP]                            ' 1-based sample index of the first low read
    LONG    measured_flt_ticks[N_REP]                       ' getct() ticks from pinfloat() to first low
    LONG    measured_bounce[N_REP]                          ' highs among BOUNCE_SAMPLES after first low
    LONG    measured_low_seen[N_REP]                        ' TRUE when the pin ever read low
    LONG    measured_pre[N_REP]                             ' 16-pin IN snapshot before the charge
    LONG    measured_post[N_REP]                            ' 16-pin IN snapshot after the probe pass

VAR { run-wide counters }

    LONG    emittedRepCount                                 ' BD-REP records emitted in the current phase

PUB main() | phase1Recs, phase2Recs
'' Run the whole board-detection characterisation sweep and tag every data point on the
'' debug stream. One fixed sequence, start to finish, with no runtime branch of any kind.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local phase1Recs - BD-REP records emitted by phase 1, the truncation detector's count
' @local phase2Recs - BD-REP records emitted by phase 2, zero when phase 2 is not compiled

    emitBannerBlock()

    emitCalibration(CAL_IDX_PRE_PHASE1)

    emittedRepCount := 0
    emitPhaseMark(1, @sMarkBegin, FALSE, 0, @sTokNA)
    runSweep(SW_COLD_NOCLR, NO_GROUP, N_REP, NO_GROUP, CST_NONE, CLR_NO)
    emitNote(@"sweep 2 follows a pinclear of every swept group -- two 8-pin calls per group per ruling R1")
    clearSweptGroups()
    runSweep(SW_COLD_CLR, NO_GROUP, N_REP, NO_GROUP, CST_NONE, CLR_YES)
    phase1Recs := emittedRepCount
    emitCalibration(CAL_IDX_POST_PHASE1)
    emitPhaseMark(1, @sMarkEnd, TRUE, phase1Recs, @sTokNA)

    phase2Recs := 0
#ifdef DETECT_PHASE2
    emitPhaseMark(2, @sMarkBegin, FALSE, 0, @sTokNA)
    emittedRepCount := 0
    runPhase2ForGroup(GRP_P0_P15, SW_LIVE_LEFT, SW_STOPPED_LEFT, SW_STOPPED_CLR_LEFT)
    runPhase2ForGroup(GRP_P16_P31, SW_LIVE_RIGHT, SW_STOPPED_RIGHT, SW_STOPPED_CLR_RIGHT)
    phase2Recs := emittedRepCount
    emitPhaseMark(2, @sMarkEnd, TRUE, phase2Recs, @sTokNA)
#else
    emitPhaseMark(2, @sMarkSkipped, FALSE, 0, @sGateNotComp)
#endif

    emitCalibration(CAL_IDX_POST_PHASE2)

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-DONE")
    lineField(@"recs", phase1Recs + phase2Recs)
    lineTextField(@"phase2", phase2Token())
    lineEmit()

    ' The literal text below is pnut-term-ts's end-of-session marker under
    ' --exit-on-end-session. It is printed exactly once, alone, as the final line, and no
    ' other output anywhere in this file may contain this phrase.
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")

PRI emitBannerBlock()
' Emit the whole banner block, once, before anything else touches a pin.

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-BANNER")
    lineField(@"fmt", FMT_VERSION)
    lineTextField(@"tool", @"test_bench_detect")
    lineTextField(@"purpose", @"getBoardType_characterization")
    lineEmit()

    emitConfigRecord()

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-CLK")
    lineField(@"clkfreq_declared", CLK_FREQ)
    lineField(@"clkfreq_runtime", CLKFREQ)
    lineTextField(@"match", flagToken(CLKFREQ == CLK_FREQ))
    lineEmit()

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-BUILD")
    lineField(@"src_rev", SRC_REV)
    lineField(@"lib_linked", LIB_LINKED)
    lineField(@"phase2_compiled", PHASE2_COMPILED)
    lineTextField(@"rail_declared", railToken())
    lineField(@"n_rep", N_REP)
    lineField(@"n_live", N_LIVE)
    lineField(@"probe_max", PROBE_MAX_ITER)
    lineField(@"cal_iter", CAL_ITER)
    lineField(@"tail_groups", TAIL_GROUPS_ON)
    lineEmit()

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-RUN")
    lineField(@"run_ct", getct())
    lineTextField(@"run_ts", @"HOSTLOG")
    lineEmit()

    emitEnumRecords()
    emitMapRecords()
    emitPlanRecords()

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-GATE")
    lineTextField(@"mark", @sMarkBuild)
    lineTextField(@"answer", gateToken())
    lineEmit()

    emitNoteRecords()

PRI emitConfigRecord()
' Emit BD-CFG. This record CANNOT lie about which config file was compiled in, because it
' is emitted from the same #ifdef BENCH_CFG that selects the OBJ. pnut-ts silently ignores
' an unknown -D (measured 2026-09-11: exit 0, binary written, no warning), so a mistyped
' -D BENCH_CFJ takes the #else arm here exactly as it does in the OBJ block and the record
' reads cfg_id,USER.

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-CFG")
#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    lineTextField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgBench)
    lineTextField(@"cfg_file", @sCfgFileBench)
#else
    lineTextField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgUser)
    lineTextField(@"cfg_file", @sCfgFileUser)
#endif
    lineField(@"motor_type", user.MOTOR_TYPE)
    lineField(@"drive_voltage", user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE)
    lineField(@"wheel_dia_x10", round(user.WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH *. 10.0))
    lineField(@"left_base", user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE)
    lineField(@"right_base", user.RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitEnumRecords() | grpIdx, grpBase, libBase
' Cross-check this binary's local base-pin table against the library's own PINS_* values.
' A match,0 on any line voids the run. In a build with no library linked every line reads
' lib,NOLIB and match,NA -- absence is a token, never a zero.
'
' @local grpIdx - index into grpEnumOrder
' @local grpBase - base pin of the group being reported
' @local libBase - the library object's value for the same group, or LIB_ABSENT

    repeat grpIdx from 0 to GROUP_COUNT - 1
        grpBase := LONG[@grpEnumOrder][grpIdx]
        libBase := libraryGroupBase(grpBase)
        lineReset()
        lineAddText(@"BD-ENUM")
        lineField(@"grp", grpBase)
        lineTextField(@"gnm", groupName(grpBase))
        lineField(@"local", grpBase)
        if libBase == LIB_ABSENT
            lineTextField(@"lib", @sVrdNoLib)
            lineTextField(@"match", @sTokNA)
        else
            lineField(@"lib", libBase)
            lineTextField(@"match", flagToken(grpBase == libBase))
        lineEmit()

PRI emitMapRecords() | grpIdx, grpBase
' Emit the sense-pin map: which physical pin each group's detection probe touches, and
' whose pin that actually is.
'
' @local grpIdx - index into grpEnumOrder
' @local grpBase - base pin of the group being reported

    repeat grpIdx from 0 to GROUP_COUNT - 1
        grpBase := LONG[@grpEnumOrder][grpIdx]
        lineReset()
        lineAddText(@"BD-MAP")
        lineField(@"grp", grpBase)
        lineTextField(@"gnm", groupName(grpBase))
        lineField(@"pin", grpBase + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET)
        lineTextField(@"ovl", overlapToken(grpBase))
        lineEmit()

PRI emitPlanRecords()
' Declare the sweep matrix before any of it runs, so the analyser can compute the expected
' BD-REP count and compare it against BD-PHASE's recs field. A truncated run then renders
' as a count mismatch rather than as silence. Sweeps 3-8 are declared only in the build
' that actually contains them, so the computed expectation is right in either build.

    emitPlanRecord(SW_COLD_NOCLR, 1, @sTokAll, N_REP, NO_GROUP, CST_NONE, CLR_NO)
    emitPlanRecord(SW_COLD_CLR, 1, @sTokAll, N_REP, NO_GROUP, CST_NONE, CLR_YES)
#ifdef DETECT_PHASE2
    emitPlanRecord(SW_LIVE_LEFT, 2, @sGrpP0P15, N_LIVE, GRP_P0_P15, CST_RUNNING, CLR_NO)
    emitPlanRecord(SW_STOPPED_LEFT, 2, @sTokAll, N_REP, GRP_P0_P15, CST_STOPPED, CLR_NO)
    emitPlanRecord(SW_STOPPED_CLR_LEFT, 2, @sTokAll, N_REP, GRP_P0_P15, CST_STOPPED, CLR_YES)
    emitPlanRecord(SW_LIVE_RIGHT, 2, @sGrpP16P31, N_LIVE, GRP_P16_P31, CST_RUNNING, CLR_NO)
    emitPlanRecord(SW_STOPPED_RIGHT, 2, @sTokAll, N_REP, GRP_P16_P31, CST_STOPPED, CLR_NO)
    emitPlanRecord(SW_STOPPED_CLR_RIGHT, 2, @sTokAll, N_REP, GRP_P16_P31, CST_STOPPED, CLR_YES)
#endif

PRI emitPlanRecord(swNum, phaseNum, pGroupSpec, nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState)
' Emit one BD-PLAN line.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param phaseNum - 1 or 2
' @param pGroupSpec - pointer to ALL or to a single group's name
' @param nRep - repeats per cell
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group a driver cog is or was running on or NO_GROUP
' @param cogState - CST_NONE / CST_RUNNING / CST_STOPPED
' @param clrState - CLR_NO / CLR_YES

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-PLAN")
    lineField(@"sw", swNum)
    lineField(@"phase", phaseNum)
    lineTextField(@"groups", pGroupSpec)
    lineField(@"n", nRep)
    lineTextField(@"cog", cogGroupToken(cogGrp))
    lineTextField(@"cogst", cogStateToken(cogState))
    lineTextField(@"clr", clearToken(clrState))
    lineEmit()

PRI emitNoteRecords()
' The operator and analyser preamble. Constant text, part of the diff alignment key: every
' one of these lines must be byte-identical between the Rev A run and the Rev B run. The
' text avoids commas so a naive field splitter cannot mistake prose for fields.

#ifdef DETECT_PHASE2
    emitNote(@"*** THIS BUILD STARTS A REAL DRIVER COG *** -- phase 2 is compiled in")
    emitNote(@"THE MOTORS MUST BE PHYSICALLY UNPLUGGED -- with no motor connected there is no current path whatever the output stage does")
    emitNote(@"PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4) and is NOT a panic button")
    emitNote(@"phase 2 starts a driver cog at commanded zero on P0_P15 then on P16_P31 and stops it; nothing is ever commanded to turn")
#elseifdef DETECT_LIB
    emitNote(@"the library isp_bldc_motor IS linked and is probed passively using testSetup() and getBoardType() -- no driver cog is started")
    emitNote(@"this binary contains no phase 2 motion code -- rebuild with -D DETECT_PHASE2 to add the cog-running sweeps")
    emitNote(@"the panic procedure at this bench is PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4)")
#else
    emitNote(@"phase 2 is NOT compiled into this build -- there is no OBJ reference to isp_bldc_motor and no driver PASM2 anywhere in this image")
    emitNote(@"this binary is therefore physically incapable of starting a driver cog; rebuild with -D DETECT_PHASE2 to add phase 2")
    emitNote(@"even so the panic procedure at this bench is PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4)")
#endif
    emitNote(@"the gate on phase 2 is compile-time only -- there is no keypress and no runtime branch anywhere in this binary")
    emitNote(@"BD-GATE answer and BD-BUILD phase2_compiled carry the same fact from two places and MUST agree; a disagreement voids the run")
    emitNote(@"sweeping a group briefly drives its base+4; with the boards at RIGHT P16_P31 and LEFT P32_P47 the gate-adjacent sense pins are P28 (right board base+12) and P44 (left board base+12)")
    emitNote(@"all six groups may be swept RAIL-OFF: P2 pins are inputs at reset so all six gate inputs already sit floating whenever no driver cog runs")
    emitNote(@"and rail-off means no bus voltage and therefore no shoot-through path whatever the gate driver does with a floating complementary input")
    emitNote(@"a RAIL-ON run should use -D DETECT_NO_TAIL which drops the two gate-adjacent tail groups")
    emitNote(@"P44 is PINS_P40_P55's sense pin and IS the LEFT board's W low-side gate input -- it is NOT unconnected; the calibration pin is P15, which is outside both board ranges")
    emitNote(@"VOID RULE: a log with no BD-BANNER or with cfg_id not equal to BENCH or with BD-CLK match 0 is VOID -- not suspect but void")
    emitNote(@"VOID RULE: any BD-ENUM match 0 voids the run -- the local pin-group table has drifted from the library's")
    emitNote(@"SUM RULE: sum 0 is real data on a Rev A board and is also what a loop that never executed produces")
    emitNote(@"SUM RULE: sum 0 is trustworthy ONLY when sumtix is at least 500 -- 500 Spin2 pinreads cannot complete in under 500 ticks")
    emitNote(@"CAL RULE: BD-CAL is emitted three times against a pin held driven high so the loop can never exit early")
    emitNote(@"CAL RULE: if the three tix_per_iter values differ by more than a few percent then every sumtix and every fltix in this log is void")
    emitNote(@"CROSS-CHECK: iter and (fltix / tix_per_iter) are two independent routes to the same number; if they disagree the instrumentation is lying")
    emitNote(@"R1 NOTE: pre and post are each assembled from TWO 8-pin pinread calls (low half in bits 0-7 high half in bits 8-15)")
    emitNote(@"R1 NOTE: that split is required because ADDPINS cannot cross a 32-pin port boundary; pre and post are therefore NOT atomic")
    emitNote(@"R1 NOTE: the lost atomicity is acceptable because pre and post are context snapshots and are not the measured interval")
    emitNote(@"HALL: bits 5 6 and 7 of a pre field are pin_hall_u/v/w so with a motor plugged in a valid 3-bit hall code is objective evidence the rail is powered")
    emitNote(@"DIFF: take the A/B diff over ^BD- lines only and exclude everything between a BD-LIB mark begin and its matching mark end")
    emitNote(@"DIFF: that exclusion is required because the library's own output line count varies with its own verdict")
    emitNote(@"DIFF: logs from different build variants are not comparable -- compare a default-build log only against another default-build log")
    emitNote(@"LIBVRD: a bare abort returns 0 and is indistinguishable from a completed call so ABORT appears only for a valued abort")
    emitNote(@"LIBVRD: ground truth for an abort is the library's own ! ERROR: line inside the BD-LIB bracket")
    emitNote(@"UNREACHABLE: cold-after-a-cog-has-run is impossible in one power cycle by definition -- that is why every cog NONE cell is phase 1")
    emitNote(@"UNREACHABLE: and it is why phase 2 can never be re-run without a reset")
    emitNote(@"UNREACHABLE: cogst RUNNING is measured only on the cog's OWN group because the cog's effect is per-pin")
    emitNote(@"UNREACHABLE: cogst RUNNING with clr CLR is meaningless and dangerous -- pinclear on a running driver's own pins destroys it -- so it is not in the matrix")
    emitNote(@"sweeps 3 and 6 deliberately charge and float a pin the running driver cog owns as an ADC smart pin -- that is exactly the T0-10 condition")
    emitNote(@"sweeps 3 and 6 are bounded at n_live rather than n_rep to minimise interference with that running cog")

PRI runSweep(swNum, groupSel, nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState) | orderIdx
' Run one sweep: either every swept group in the fixed tail-last order or a single group.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param groupSel - base pin of the only group to sweep or NO_GROUP for all swept groups
' @param nRep - repeats per cell
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group a driver cog is or was running on or NO_GROUP
' @param cogState - CST_NONE / CST_RUNNING / CST_STOPPED
' @param clrState - CLR_NO / CLR_YES
'
' @local orderIdx - index into grpSweepOrder

    emitSweepMark(swNum, @sMarkBegin)
    if groupSel == NO_GROUP
        repeat orderIdx from 0 to SWEPT_GROUP_COUNT - 1
            runCell(swNum, LONG[@grpSweepOrder][orderIdx], nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState)
    else
        runCell(swNum, groupSel, nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState)
    emitSweepMark(swNum, @sMarkEnd)

PRI runCell(swNum, grpBase, nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState) | repIdx, libVerdict
' Measure one cell of the matrix -- nRep repeats on one group -- then emit every repeat,
' then probe the library on the same group, then summarise. Measurement first and emission
' second is deliberate: no debug() may land inside a measured interval.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group under measurement
' @param nRep - repeats in this cell
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group a driver cog is or was running on or NO_GROUP
' @param cogState - CST_NONE / CST_RUNNING / CST_STOPPED
' @param clrState - CLR_NO / CLR_YES
'
' @local repIdx - repeat index within this cell
' @local libVerdict - VRD_* the library itself returned for this group

    repeat repIdx from 0 to nRep - 1
        measureOneRepeat(grpBase, repIdx)

    repeat repIdx from 0 to nRep - 1
        emitRepeatRecord(swNum, grpBase, repIdx, cogGrp, cogState, clrState)

    libVerdict := runLibraryProbe(swNum, grpBase)
    emitCellSummary(swNum, grpBase, nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState, libVerdict)

PRI measureOneRepeat(grpBase, repIdx) | sensePin, pinSum, ctBefore, ctAfter, iterCount, lastLevel, bounceCnt, sampleIdx, bLowSeen
' Take one repeat: the library's own 500-read sum pass and then, with its own fresh charge,
' the first-low probe pass. The two passes never share state. Results go into the VAR
' arrays; nothing is printed.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group under measurement
' @param repIdx - slot in the VAR capture arrays to fill
'
' @local sensePin - grpBase + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET, exactly as getBoardType() computes it
' @local pinSum - running sum of the 500 pinread results
' @local ctBefore - getct() immediately before a measured loop
' @local ctAfter - getct() immediately after a measured loop
' @local iterCount - 1-based count of first-low probe samples taken
' @local lastLevel - the most recent pinread result in the probe loop
' @local bounceCnt - highs seen among BOUNCE_SAMPLES after first-low
' @local sampleIdx - index over the post-first-low bounce samples
' @local bLowSeen - TRUE when the probe loop exited because the pin read low

    sensePin := grpBase + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET
    measured_pre[repIdx] := snapshotGroupPins(grpBase)

    ' Pass one is a transcription of isp_bldc_motor.spin2:776-784 with the two debug()
    ' calls removed and two getct() calls added OUTSIDE the repeat. The loop body is one
    ' statement, character-for-character the library's. Nothing is added inside the
    ' measured interval.
    pinSum := 0
    pinhigh(sensePin)                                       ' charge 0.1uF capacitor on RevB boards
    waitms(CHARGE_MS)
    pinfloat(sensePin)                                      ' release the pin, ready to read state
    ctBefore := getct()
    repeat SUM_ITER
        pinSum += pinread(sensePin)
    ctAfter := getct()
    measured_sum[repIdx] := pinSum
    measured_sum_ticks[repIdx] := ctAfter - ctBefore

    ' Pass two is the measurement that is the point: the sample index and the tick delta at
    ' which the pin FIRST reads low -- the real RC discharge time, convertible to
    ' microseconds and clock-independent. The 500-read sum is clock-dependent by the
    ' library's own comment at isp_bldc_motor.spin2:787. During this probe the pin is
    ' floating and not driven, so a long probe on an empty group is electrically inert.
    pinhigh(sensePin)
    waitms(CHARGE_MS)
    pinfloat(sensePin)
    ctBefore := getct()
    iterCount := 0
    repeat
        lastLevel := pinread(sensePin)
        iterCount += 1
    until (lastLevel == 0) or (iterCount == PROBE_MAX_ITER)
    ctAfter := getct()

    bLowSeen := (lastLevel == 0)
    measured_iter[repIdx] := iterCount
    measured_flt_ticks[repIdx] := ctAfter - ctBefore
    measured_low_seen[repIdx] := bLowSeen

    ' Everything below is AFTER ctAfter and so cannot perturb the measured interval. A
    ' clean RC discharge bounces zero times; a floating pin flapping at the input threshold
    ' bounces well above zero, which is the expected discriminator for the false positive
    ' seen on the empty P32_P47 group.
    bounceCnt := 0
    if bLowSeen == TRUE
        repeat sampleIdx from 1 to BOUNCE_SAMPLES
            if pinread(sensePin) <> 0
                bounceCnt += 1
    measured_bounce[repIdx] := bounceCnt
    measured_post[repIdx] := snapshotGroupPins(grpBase)

PRI emitRepeatRecord(swNum, grpBase, repIdx, cogGrp, cogState, clrState)
' Emit one BD-REP line for one captured repeat. The three first-low fields are numbers when
' the pin went low and the tokens NEVER / NEVER / NOMEAS when it never did -- they are
' never independently absent, because all three come from the same single fact.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group under measurement
' @param repIdx - slot in the VAR capture arrays to report
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group a driver cog is or was running on or NO_GROUP
' @param cogState - CST_NONE / CST_RUNNING / CST_STOPPED
' @param clrState - CLR_NO / CLR_YES

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-REP")
    lineField(@"sw", swNum)
    lineField(@"grp", grpBase)
    lineTextField(@"gnm", groupName(grpBase))
    lineField(@"pin", grpBase + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET)
    lineTextField(@"ovl", overlapToken(grpBase))
    lineField(@"rep", repIdx + 1)
    lineTextField(@"cog", cogGroupToken(cogGrp))
    lineTextField(@"cogst", cogStateToken(cogState))
    lineTextField(@"clr", clearToken(clrState))
    lineField(@"sum", measured_sum[repIdx])
    lineField(@"sumtix", measured_sum_ticks[repIdx])
    lineTextField(@"vrd", verdictToken(verdictForSum(measured_sum[repIdx], measured_sum_ticks[repIdx])))
    if measured_low_seen[repIdx] == TRUE
        lineField(@"iter", measured_iter[repIdx])
        lineField(@"fltix", measured_flt_ticks[repIdx])
        lineField(@"bnc", measured_bounce[repIdx])
        lineTextField(@"exit", @sExitLow)
    else
        lineTextField(@"iter", @sTokNever)
        lineTextField(@"fltix", @sTokNever)
        lineTextField(@"bnc", @sTokNoMeas)
        lineTextField(@"exit", @sExitMaxed)
    lineHexField(@"pre", measured_pre[repIdx])
    lineHexField(@"post", measured_post[repIdx])
    lineEmit()

    emittedRepCount += 1

PRI emitCellSummary(swNum, grpBase, nRep, cogGrp, cogState, clrState, libVerdict) | repIdx, sumMin, sumMax, sumTotal, cntA, cntB, cntN, modalVrd, flMin, flMax, flNever, bncMax
' Summarise one cell. agree compares the library's verdict against this cell's modal
' replica verdict -- that is the honesty check on the replica, and a wrong replica renders
' as agree,0. It is a check that can genuinely fail.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group under measurement
' @param nRep - repeats in this cell
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group a driver cog is or was running on or NO_GROUP
' @param cogState - CST_NONE / CST_RUNNING / CST_STOPPED
' @param clrState - CLR_NO / CLR_YES
' @param libVerdict - VRD_* the library itself returned for this group
'
' @local repIdx - repeat index within this cell
' @local sumMin - smallest pinSum seen in this cell
' @local sumMax - largest pinSum seen in this cell
' @local sumTotal - running total of pinSum used to derive the mean
' @local cntA - repeats whose replica verdict was VRD_REVA
' @local cntB - repeats whose replica verdict was VRD_REVB
' @local cntN - repeats whose replica verdict was VRD_NODET
' @local modalVrd - majority replica verdict for this cell or VRD_TIE
' @local flMin - smallest first-low sample index among repeats that went low
' @local flMax - largest first-low sample index among repeats that went low
' @local flNever - repeats whose pin never read low
' @local bncMax - largest bounce count among repeats that went low

    sumMin := POSX
    sumMax := NEGX
    sumTotal := 0
    cntA := 0
    cntB := 0
    cntN := 0
    flMin := POSX
    flMax := NEGX
    flNever := 0
    bncMax := 0

    repeat repIdx from 0 to nRep - 1
        sumMin := sumMin <# measured_sum[repIdx]
        sumMax := sumMax #> measured_sum[repIdx]
        sumTotal += measured_sum[repIdx]
        case verdictForSum(measured_sum[repIdx], measured_sum_ticks[repIdx])
            VRD_REVA:
                cntA += 1
            VRD_REVB:
                cntB += 1
            VRD_NODET:
                cntN += 1
        if measured_low_seen[repIdx] == TRUE
            flMin := flMin <# measured_iter[repIdx]
            flMax := flMax #> measured_iter[repIdx]
            bncMax := bncMax #> measured_bounce[repIdx]
        else
            flNever += 1

    modalVrd := modalVerdict(cntA, cntB, cntN)

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-CELL")
    lineField(@"sw", swNum)
    lineField(@"grp", grpBase)
    lineTextField(@"gnm", groupName(grpBase))
    lineTextField(@"cog", cogGroupToken(cogGrp))
    lineTextField(@"cogst", cogStateToken(cogState))
    lineTextField(@"clr", clearToken(clrState))
    lineField(@"n", nRep)
    lineField(@"sum_min", sumMin)
    lineField(@"sum_max", sumMax)
    lineField(@"sum_mean", sumTotal / nRep)
    lineField(@"va", cntA)
    lineField(@"vb", cntB)
    lineField(@"vn", cntN)
    lineTextField(@"modal", verdictToken(modalVrd))
    if flNever == nRep
        lineTextField(@"fl_min", @sTokNever)
        lineTextField(@"fl_max", @sTokNever)
        lineField(@"fl_never", flNever)
        lineTextField(@"bnc_max", @sTokNoMeas)
    else
        lineField(@"fl_min", flMin)
        lineField(@"fl_max", flMax)
        lineField(@"fl_never", flNever)
        lineField(@"bnc_max", bncMax)
    lineTextField(@"libvrd", verdictToken(libVerdict))
    lineTextField(@"agree", agreeToken(libVerdict, modalVrd))
    lineEmit()

PRI isCalPinSafe() : bSafe
' TRUE when CAL_PIN lies outside BOTH declared motor pin ranges, so driving it high cannot
' reach a gate-driver input. Checked against the declared bases at runtime rather than
' assumed, because the previous CAL_PIN was chosen under a wrong belief about where the
' boards were and silently became a gate pin when that was corrected.
'
' @returns bSafe - TRUE when the calibration pin is electrically dead on this configuration

    bSafe := not (pinIsInsideGroup(CAL_PIN, user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE) or pinIsInsideGroup(CAL_PIN, user.RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE))

PRI emitCalibration(calIdx) | ctBefore, ctAfter, iterCount, lastLevel, elapsedTix
' Run the first-low poll loop's exact shape against a pin held DRIVEN HIGH so it can never
' exit early, and report ticks per iteration. That number is the resolution error bar on
' every fltix in this log. Emitted three times -- before phase 1, after phase 1, after
' phase 2 -- and if the three differ by more than a few percent every sumtix and fltix in
' the log is void. The iter field reports the count ACTUALLY reached rather than the
' constant CAL_ITER, so an early exit is visible instead of being asserted away.
'
' @param calIdx - CAL_IDX_* identifying which of the three calibrations this is
'
' @local ctBefore - getct() immediately before the calibration loop
' @local ctAfter - getct() immediately after the calibration loop
' @local iterCount - calibration loop iterations actually executed
' @local lastLevel - the most recent pinread result in the calibration loop
' @local elapsedTix - ctAfter - ctBefore

    if not isCalPinSafe()
        lineReset()
        lineAddText(@"BD-CAL")
        lineField(@"idx", calIdx)
        lineField(@"iter", 0)
        lineTextField(@"tix", @sTokNoMeas)
        lineTextField(@"tix_per_iter", @sTokNoMeas)
        lineEmit()
        emitNote(@"CAL SKIPPED -- CAL_PIN falls inside a declared board's pin range and would drive a gate input")
        return

    pinhigh(CAL_PIN)
    ctBefore := getct()
    iterCount := 0
    repeat
        lastLevel := pinread(CAL_PIN)
        iterCount += 1
    until (lastLevel == 0) or (iterCount == CAL_ITER)
    ctAfter := getct()
    pinfloat(CAL_PIN)

    elapsedTix := ctAfter - ctBefore
    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-CAL")
    lineField(@"idx", calIdx)
    lineField(@"iter", iterCount)
    lineField(@"tix", elapsedTix)
    lineField(@"tix_per_iter", elapsedTix / iterCount)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitPhaseMark(phaseNum, pMarkName, bHasRecs, recCount, pReason)
' Emit one BD-PHASE line. recs is a number only on a mark that has actually counted
' records; otherwise it is the token NOMEAS.
'
' @param phaseNum - 1 or 2
' @param pMarkName - pointer to begin / end / skipped
' @param bHasRecs - TRUE when recCount is meaningful
' @param recCount - BD-REP records emitted in this phase
' @param pReason - pointer to NA or to a reason token

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-PHASE")
    lineField(@"n", phaseNum)
    lineTextField(@"mark", pMarkName)
    if bHasRecs == TRUE
        lineField(@"recs", recCount)
    else
        lineTextField(@"recs", @sTokNoMeas)
    lineTextField(@"reason", pReason)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSweepMark(swNum, pMarkName)
' Emit one BD-SWEEP line.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param pMarkName - pointer to begin or end

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-SWEEP")
    lineField(@"sw", swNum)
    lineTextField(@"mark", pMarkName)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitNote(pNoteText)
' Emit one BD-NOTE line. Constant operator/analyser text, one clause per line.
'
' @param pNoteText - pointer to the note text

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-NOTE,")
    lineAddText(pNoteText)
    lineEmit()

PRI clearSweptGroups() | orderIdx
' pinclear every group this build sweeps. The four electrically-safe groups already span
' P0-P55 between them so the tail groups add no pins here.
'
' @local orderIdx - index into grpSweepOrder

    repeat orderIdx from 0 to SWEPT_GROUP_COUNT - 1
        clearGroupPins(LONG[@grpSweepOrder][orderIdx])

PRI clearGroupPins(grpBase)
' Clear all sixteen of a group's pins as TWO 8-pin operations. See ruling R1: ADDPINS
' cannot cross a 32-pin port boundary, and pinclear(24 addpins 15) would have wrapped and
' cleared the LEFT board's P0-P7 -- its ADC and hall pins -- silently contaminating the
' very axis being measured.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to clear

    pinclear(grpBase addpins HALF_GROUP_SPAN)
    pinclear(grpBase + GROUP_HI_OFFSET addpins HALF_GROUP_SPAN)

PRI snapshotGroupPins(grpBase) : pinBits
' Read all sixteen of a group's IN bits as TWO 8-pin reads, low half in bits 0-7 and high
' half in bits 8-15. Split for the same ADDPINS reason as clearGroupPins(). The two halves
' are therefore NOT sampled atomically -- acceptable because pre and post are context
' snapshots and not the measured interval.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to snapshot
' @returns pinBits - the group's sixteen IN bits

    pinBits := pinread(grpBase addpins HALF_GROUP_SPAN)
    pinBits |= pinread(grpBase + GROUP_HI_OFFSET addpins HALF_GROUP_SPAN) << HIGH_HALF_SHIFT

PRI verdictForSum(pinSum, sumTicks) : verdictCode | highTimeUs
' The library getBoardType() verdict cascade, in the same order and with the same integer
' arithmetic, so a sum of exactly 250 or 251, or a high time of exactly 19 or 20 uS, lands
' where the library lands it: sum 0 REVA, sum > 250 NODET, high time < 20 uS NODET, else REVB.
' High time is pinSum x (loop ticks / SUM_ITER) in microseconds, from the sumtix this file
' already records around the same loop.
'
' @param pinSum - the 500-pinread sum
' @param sumTicks - ticks the 500-pinread loop took (sumtix)
' @returns verdictCode - VRD_REVA / VRD_REVB / VRD_NODET
'
' @local highTimeUs - how long the released pin stayed high, in microseconds

    highTimeUs := (pinSum * sumTicks / SUM_ITER) / ((CLKFREQ / USEC_PER_SEC) #> 1)
    if pinSum == 0
        verdictCode := VRD_REVA
    elseif pinSum > REVB_SUM_LIMIT
        verdictCode := VRD_NODET
    elseif highTimeUs < REVB_MIN_US
        verdictCode := VRD_NODET
    else
        verdictCode := VRD_REVB

PRI modalVerdict(cntA, cntB, cntN) : verdictCode
' Return the majority replica verdict for a cell or VRD_TIE when no single verdict leads.
'
' @param cntA - repeats whose replica verdict was VRD_REVA
' @param cntB - repeats whose replica verdict was VRD_REVB
' @param cntN - repeats whose replica verdict was VRD_NODET
' @returns verdictCode - VRD_REVA / VRD_REVB / VRD_NODET / VRD_TIE

    verdictCode := VRD_TIE
    if (cntA > cntB) and (cntA > cntN)
        verdictCode := VRD_REVA
    elseif (cntB > cntA) and (cntB > cntN)
        verdictCode := VRD_REVB
    elseif (cntN > cntA) and (cntN > cntB)
        verdictCode := VRD_NODET

PRI runLibraryProbe(swNum, grpBase) : libVerdict | trappedLib, eBoardRev
' Bracket the library's own detection output and report the verdict IT returned. The
' library's "--- pinSum = N, 64010 Rev X" line lands between the markers; this method does
' not reprint it, and the A/B diff excludes everything between the markers because the
' library's line count varies with its own verdict.
'
' @param swNum - SW_* identifier of this sweep
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to probe
' @returns libVerdict - VRD_* the library returned
'
' @local trappedLib - the trapped return of the library setup call; a bare abort returns 0
'                      and is indistinguishable from a completed call
' @local eBoardRev - the library's REV_* return value

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-LIB")
    lineField(@"sw", swNum)
    lineField(@"grp", grpBase)
    lineTextField(@"mark", @sMarkBegin)
    lineEmit()

    libVerdict := VRD_NOLIB
    trappedLib := 0
    eBoardRev := 0
#ifdef DETECT_LIB
    ' One shared instance is used for every probe and for phase 2. claimPinBase() releases
    ' this instance's own claim before re-claiming, so walking every group on one instance
    ' never self-conflicts -- and a second instance could not be used, because it would
    ' collide with this one's claim on exactly the groups that matter most.
    trappedLib := \motor.testSetup(grpBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    if trappedLib <> 0
        libVerdict := VRD_ABORT
    elseif not isLegalLibraryBase(grpBase)
        ' PINS_NO_USE_P24_P39 is rejected by validatePinBase()'s lookdown, so pinbase stays
        ' unset and getBoardType() takes its "** NOT SET **" branch without ever measuring.
        ' The illegal group is reachable only through the replica -- a documented property
        ' of today's code, not a defect this binary is asked to fix.
        libVerdict := VRD_NOBASE
    else
        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        case eBoardRev
            motor.REV_A:
                libVerdict := VRD_REVA
            motor.REV_B:
                libVerdict := VRD_REVB
            motor.REV_Unknown:
                libVerdict := VRD_NODET
            other:
                libVerdict := VRD_UNKNOWN
#endif

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-LIB")
    lineField(@"sw", swNum)
    lineField(@"grp", grpBase)
    lineTextField(@"mark", @sMarkEnd)
    lineTextField(@"libvrd", verdictToken(libVerdict))
    lineField(@"trapped", trappedLib)
    lineEmit()

#ifdef DETECT_PHASE2

PRI runPhase2ForGroup(cogGrp, swLive, swStopped, swStoppedClr)
' Phase 2 for one group: start a real driver cog at commanded zero, sweep the group while
' it runs, stop it, sweep every group immediately afterwards, pinclear and sweep again.
' This is the only thing that separates "the threshold is wrong" from "stop() clears only
' the top 8 pins and poisons the next read" -- two diagnoses that want opposite fixes.
'
' start() is called with BRD_REV_B FORCED rather than BRD_AUTO_DET so getBoardType() takes
' its early-out and the cog start performs no charge/float of its own, isolating the cog's
' pin-configuration effect from the detection measurement.
'
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group to run a driver cog on
' @param swLive - SW_* identifier of the cog-running sweep
' @param swStopped - SW_* identifier of the post-stop sweep
' @param swStoppedClr - SW_* identifier of the post-stop pinclear'd sweep

    emitPhase2Step(cogGrp, @sPh2Pre)
    emitPhase2Step(cogGrp, @sPh2Starting)
    startDriverCog(cogGrp)
    waitms(SETTLE_MS)
    emitPhase2Step(cogGrp, @sPh2Running)

    runSweep(swLive, cogGrp, N_LIVE, cogGrp, CST_RUNNING, CLR_NO)

    emitPhase2Step(cogGrp, @sPh2Stopping)
    motor.stop()
    ' The pins field of the record below is the within-a-millisecond-of-stop() snapshot of
    ' the driver's own group. The sweep that follows walks the groups in the fixed
    ' tail-last order, so for the right-hand group its own cell is not the first one taken
    ' after stop() -- this record is where that immediate observation lives.
    emitPhase2Step(cogGrp, @sPh2Stopped)

    runSweep(swStopped, NO_GROUP, N_REP, cogGrp, CST_STOPPED, CLR_NO)
    clearSweptGroups()
    runSweep(swStoppedClr, NO_GROUP, N_REP, cogGrp, CST_STOPPED, CLR_YES)

PRI startDriverCog(cogGrp) | startRet, rawMotorCog
' Start the driver cog on {cogGrp} at commanded zero and report both start()'s raw return
' and the object's own motorCog snapshot, because start()'s return alone has been observed
' to read 0 on a call that genuinely started a cog.
'
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group to run a driver cog on
'
' @local startRet - start()'s trapped raw return value
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot of the object's own motorCog

    startRet := \motor.start(cogGrp, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_REV_B)
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-PH2")
    lineField(@"grp", cogGrp)
    lineTextField(@"step", @sPh2Started)
    lineTextField(@"detmode", @"BRD_REV_B")
    lineField(@"start_ret", startRet)
    lineField(@"motorcog", rawMotorCog)
    lineHexField(@"pins", snapshotGroupPins(cogGrp))
    lineEmit()

PRI emitPhase2Step(cogGrp, pStepName)
' Emit one BD-PH2 record for a step that carries no start() return of its own.
'
' @param cogGrp - base pin of the group to run a driver cog on
' @param pStepName - pointer to the step-name token

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BD-PH2")
    lineField(@"grp", cogGrp)
    lineTextField(@"step", pStepName)
    lineTextField(@"detmode", @"BRD_REV_B")
    lineTextField(@"start_ret", @sTokNoMeas)
    lineTextField(@"motorcog", @sTokNoMeas)
    lineHexField(@"pins", snapshotGroupPins(cogGrp))
    lineEmit()

#endif

PRI isLegalLibraryBase(grpBase) : bLegal
' Replicate validatePinBase()'s lookdown list so the NOBASE case is decided the way the
' library decides it rather than by hardcoding one group number.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to test
' @returns bLegal - TRUE when the library accepts this base

    bLegal := (grpBase == GRP_P0_P15) or (grpBase == GRP_P8_P23) or (grpBase == GRP_P16_P31) or (grpBase == GRP_P32_P47) or (grpBase == GRP_P40_P55)


PRI libraryGroupBase(grpBase) : libBase
' Return the library object's OWN PINS_* value for a group, or LIB_ABSENT when the library
' is not linked into this build. This is the cross-check behind BD-ENUM: if the library's
' enum ever moves, the local table stops matching and the run is voided.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to look up in the local table
' @returns libBase - the library's value for the same group or LIB_ABSENT

    libBase := LIB_ABSENT
#ifdef DETECT_LIB
    case grpBase
        GRP_P0_P15:
            libBase := motor.PINS_P0_P15
        GRP_P8_P23:
            libBase := motor.PINS_P8_P23
        GRP_P16_P31:
            libBase := motor.PINS_P16_P31
        GRP_P24_P39:
            libBase := motor.PINS_NO_USE_P24_P39
        GRP_P32_P47:
            libBase := motor.PINS_P32_P47
        GRP_P40_P55:
            libBase := motor.PINS_P40_P55
#endif

PRI groupName(grpBase) : pGrpName
' Return the printable name of a pin group.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to name
' @returns pGrpName - pointer to the group's name string

    pGrpName := @sTokUnknown
    case grpBase
        GRP_P0_P15:
            pGrpName := @sGrpP0P15
        GRP_P8_P23:
            pGrpName := @sGrpP8P23
        GRP_P16_P31:
            pGrpName := @sGrpP16P31
        GRP_P24_P39:
            pGrpName := @sGrpP24P39
        GRP_P32_P47:
            pGrpName := @sGrpP32P47
        GRP_P40_P55:
            pGrpName := @sGrpP40P55

PRI overlapClass(grpBase) : ovlCode | sensePin
' Classify whose pin a group's sense pin actually is, at RUNTIME from the active config's
' LEFT_MOTOR_BASE and RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE -- never hardcoded. On the bench config this makes
' P8_P23's sense pin P12 the LEFT board's W low-side gate input and NO_USE_P24_P39's sense
' pin P28 the RIGHT board's, which is exactly why those two groups are swept last.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group being classified
' @returns ovlCode - OVL_SELF / OVL_NONE / OVL_LEFT_PWM / OVL_RIGHT_PWM / OVL_OTHER
'
' @local sensePin - grpBase + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET

    sensePin := grpBase + SENSE_PIN_OFFSET
    if (grpBase == user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE) or (grpBase == user.RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE)
        ovlCode := OVL_SELF
    elseif pinIsInsideGroup(sensePin, user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE)
        ovlCode := (sensePin - user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE == PWM_W_L_OFFSET) ? OVL_LEFT_PWM : OVL_OTHER
    elseif pinIsInsideGroup(sensePin, user.RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE)
        ovlCode := (sensePin - user.RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE == PWM_W_L_OFFSET) ? OVL_RIGHT_PWM : OVL_OTHER
    else
        ovlCode := OVL_NONE

PRI pinIsInsideGroup(pinNum, grpBase) : bInside
' Test whether a pin falls inside a sixteen-pin motor group.
'
' @param pinNum - the pin to test
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group to test against
' @returns bInside - TRUE when pinNum lies in grpBase..grpBase+15

    bInside := (pinNum >= grpBase) and (pinNum < grpBase + GROUP_SPAN)

PRI overlapToken(grpBase) : pOvlTok
' Return the printable overlap classification for a group's sense pin.
'
' @param grpBase - base pin of the group being classified
' @returns pOvlTok - pointer to the overlap token string

    pOvlTok := @sOvlOther
    case overlapClass(grpBase)
        OVL_SELF:
            pOvlTok := @sOvlSelf
        OVL_NONE:
            pOvlTok := @sOvlNone
        OVL_LEFT_PWM:
            pOvlTok := @sOvlLeftPwm
        OVL_RIGHT_PWM:
            pOvlTok := @sOvlRightPwm

PRI verdictToken(verdictCode) : pVrdTok
' Return the printable form of a VRD_* verdict code.
'
' @param verdictCode - VRD_* code to render
' @returns pVrdTok - pointer to the verdict token string

    pVrdTok := @sTokUnknown
    case verdictCode
        VRD_REVA:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdRevA
        VRD_REVB:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdRevB
        VRD_NODET:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdNoDet
        VRD_TIE:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdTie
        VRD_UNKNOWN:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdUnknown
        VRD_NOBASE:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdNoBase
        VRD_ABORT:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdAbort
        VRD_NOLIB:
            pVrdTok := @sVrdNoLib

PRI cogGroupToken(cogGrp) : pCogTok
' Return the printable name of the group a driver cog is or was running on.
'
' @param cogGrp - base pin of that group or NO_GROUP
' @returns pCogTok - pointer to the token string

    pCogTok := (cogGrp == NO_GROUP) ? @sCstNone : groupName(cogGrp)

PRI cogStateToken(cogState) : pStateTok
' Return the printable form of a CST_* cog-state code.
'
' @param cogState - CST_NONE / CST_RUNNING / CST_STOPPED
' @returns pStateTok - pointer to the token string

    pStateTok := @sCstNone
    case cogState
        CST_RUNNING:
            pStateTok := @sCstRunning
        CST_STOPPED:
            pStateTok := @sCstStopped

PRI clearToken(clrState) : pClrTok
' Return the printable form of a CLR_* pinclear-axis code.
'
' @param clrState - CLR_NO / CLR_YES
' @returns pClrTok - pointer to the token string

    pClrTok := (clrState == CLR_YES) ? @sClrYes : @sClrNo

PRI flagToken(bCond) : pFlagTok
' Return "1" or "0" for a boolean, so a fixed-field record never has to change shape to
' carry a yes/no answer.
'
' @param bCond - the condition to render
' @returns pFlagTok - pointer to the token string

    pFlagTok := (bCond == TRUE) ? @sFlagTrue : @sFlagFalse

PRI agreeToken(libVerdict, modalVrd) : pAgreeTok
' Compare the library's verdict against this cell's modal replica verdict. NA whenever the
' library produced no comparable verdict at all; otherwise a 1 or a 0 that can genuinely
' come out 0 -- this is the honesty check on the replica.
'
' @param libVerdict - VRD_* the library returned
' @param modalVrd - VRD_* majority replica verdict for the cell
' @returns pAgreeTok - pointer to the token string

    if (libVerdict == VRD_REVA) or (libVerdict == VRD_REVB) or (libVerdict == VRD_NODET)
        pAgreeTok := flagToken(libVerdict == modalVrd)
    else
        pAgreeTok := @sTokNA

PRI railToken() : pRailTok
' Return the printable form of the operator's compile-time rail declaration.
'
' @returns pRailTok - pointer to the token string

    pRailTok := @sRailUndecl
    case RAIL_DECLARED
        RAIL_ON:
            pRailTok := @sRailOn
        RAIL_OFF:
            pRailTok := @sRailOff

PRI gateToken() : pGateTok
' Return COMPILED or NOTCOMPILED, the whole of what the phase-2 gate now is.
'
' @returns pGateTok - pointer to the token string

    pGateTok := (PHASE2_COMPILED == 1) ? @sGateCompiled : @sGateNotComp

PRI phase2Token() : pPhaseTok
' Return RAN or NOTCOMPILED for the BD-DONE record.
'
' @returns pPhaseTok - pointer to the token string

    pPhaseTok := (PHASE2_COMPILED == 1) ? @sPhase2Ran : @sGateNotComp

PRI lineReset()
' Begin a new record.

    lineLen := 0
    BYTE[@lineBuf][0] := 0

PRI lineAddChar(charByte)
' Append one character to the record under assembly, silently dropping anything past the
' buffer. The widest record is well under LINE_BUF_SIZE; truncation would show as a short
' line in the log rather than as memory corruption.
'
' @param charByte - the character to append

    if lineLen < LINE_BUF_SIZE - 1
        BYTE[@lineBuf][lineLen] := charByte
        lineLen += 1
        BYTE[@lineBuf][lineLen] := 0

PRI lineAddText(pText) | srcIdx
' Append a zero-terminated string to the record under assembly. The loop is bounded as
' well as terminated: an unterminated source string would otherwise spin forever and hang
' a bench run with no output at all, which is the one failure mode a one-shot rig cannot
' afford. Every caller passes a DAT or literal string, so the bound should never bite.
'
' @param pText - pointer to the text to append
'
' @local srcIdx - index into the source text

    repeat srcIdx from 0 to LINE_BUF_SIZE - 1
        if BYTE[pText][srcIdx] == 0
            quit
        lineAddChar(BYTE[pText][srcIdx])

PRI lineAddNum(numValue) | digitStack[MAX_DEC_DIGITS], digitCount, absValue, digitIdx
' Append a signed decimal number with an underscore every three digits, matching the
' grouping udec_() and sdec_() use everywhere else in this tree's bench logs.
'
' @param numValue - the value to append
'
' @local digitStack - decimal digits of numValue, least significant first
' @local digitCount - how many entries of digitStack are in use
' @local absValue - magnitude of numValue, consumed by the extraction loop
' @local digitIdx - index into digitStack while emitting

    absValue := numValue
    if numValue < 0
        lineAddChar("-")
        absValue := -numValue

    digitCount := 0
    repeat
        digitStack[digitCount] := absValue // DEC_RADIX
        absValue /= DEC_RADIX
        digitCount += 1
    until (absValue == 0) or (digitCount == MAX_DEC_DIGITS)

    repeat digitIdx from digitCount - 1 to 0
        lineAddChar("0" + digitStack[digitIdx])
        if (digitIdx > 0) and (digitIdx // DIGITS_PER_GROUP == 0)
            lineAddChar("_")

PRI lineAddHex4(hexValue) | nibIdx, nibble
' Append a four-digit hex value with a leading dollar sign.
'
' @param hexValue - the value to append, low 16 bits used
'
' @local nibIdx - index of the nibble being emitted, most significant first
' @local nibble - the nibble's value

    lineAddChar("$")
    repeat nibIdx from HEX4_DIGITS - 1 to 0
        nibble := (hexValue >> (nibIdx * BITS_PER_NIBBLE)) & NIBBLE_MASK
        if nibble < DEC_RADIX
            lineAddChar("0" + nibble)
        else
            lineAddChar("A" + nibble - DEC_RADIX)

PRI lineField(pFieldName, numValue)
' Append one ",name,<number>" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param numValue - the field's value

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddNum(numValue)

PRI lineTextField(pFieldName, pFieldValue)
' Append one ",name,<token>" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param pFieldValue - pointer to the field's token text

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldValue)

PRI lineHexField(pFieldName, hexValue)
' Append one ",name,$HHHH" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param hexValue - the field's value, low 16 bits used

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddHex4(hexValue)

PRI lineEmit()
' Emit the assembled record as exactly one debug line. One debug() statement carries at
' most 255 bytes of debug data, which the wider records overrun by a factor of three, so
' the whole record travels as a single zero-terminated string instead.

    debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))

